], "overall": "A faithful, close translation that keeps the Septuagintal oddities, e.g. 'não exacerbou as suas palavras' (v. 28), 'Fez das chuvas deles granizo' (v. 32) and 'mosca canina' (v. 31). The one real fault is v. 6, where 'servi ejus' (Abraham his servant) has become plural 'seus servos'. The other items are minor tightenings. The pointing marks match the Latin in every verse: one mediant each, no flex or second mediant, and v. 18 has its mediant after 'alma'."}
